{
  "name": "Improved Brutal Strike",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You have honed new ways to attack furiously. The following effects are now among your Brutal Strike options.</p><ul><li><strong>Staggering Blow.</strong> The target must succeed on a CON Saving Throw or have Disadvantage on the next Saving Throw it makes, and it can't take Bonus Actions or Reactions until the start of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Sundering Blow.</strong> Before the start of your next turn, the next Attack Roll made by another creature against the target gains a +5 bonus to the roll. If the attack hits, the attacker can maximize up to two of its damage dice. An Attack Roll can gain only one Sundering Blow bonus.</li></ul>",
